{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011PsE52UqcqGhpZ67U7Spb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the numbers look weird:\n\nBefore: STARK excl trace = 1292ms, LogUp GKR = 528ms\nAfter (v2 with coalesced intermediates): STARK excl trace = 1466ms, LogUp GKR = 694ms\n\nThat's STILL a big regression: +166ms on LogUp GKR, +174ms on STARK excl trace.\n\nBut the input_evals phase itself improved (230ms + 252ms = 482ms total across segments). \n\nWait, the issue is that the TOTAL LogUp GKR is 694ms. \n\nSo even though the input_evals got faster, the overall GKR time went from 528ms to 694ms—that's a 166ms regression. The intermediates are massive at 576 MB and 443 MB, and I suspect the batched kernel is just slower because of the memory overhead, even with the coalescing optimization.\n\nThe old approach used 8 threads with a shared buffer of about 335 MB total, where each thread reused the same buffer across all 26 AIRs it processed. The batched code allocates separate intermediate regions for all 211 AIRs, so while the total write volume is identical, the memory footprint and access patterns are fundamentally different—and apparently much slower.\n\nThe real issue is cache behavior: the old code's per-AIR kernel launches kept the intermediates buffer hot in L2 cache between consecutive AIRs on the same thread, but the batched approach spreads all AIRs across different memory regions simultaneously, causing L2 thrashing since the cache can't hold all of them at once. The concurrent execution across different AIRs with different intermediate regions is what's killing performance here.\n\nGiven that the intermediates buffer dominates memory traffic and sequential per-AIR execution already provides good cache reuse with the existing 8-stream approach, batching these global AIRs doesn't actually help—the optimization fundamentally doesn't work when the buffer size is large because it prevents the cache reuse that makes the current approach efficient.\n\nI'm reconsidering whether to try an even more aggressive threshold, batching only AIRs with very small heights where intermediates might fit in L2 cache, but the math shows this won't work either—even 10% of the 211 batch-eligible AIRs would exceed the RTX 4090's 72 MB L2 cache given the total 576 MB of intermediates across all candidates.\n\nInstead, I'll try a simpler approach: cap the total intermediates across a batch at 64 MB to stay within L2 limits, and skip batching entirely if that threshold would be exceeded.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":110065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1046},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aecb5aa0-2278-4de6-b698-d4c309499c34","uuid":"6e1e520c-7842-4c60-9c48-81c757f0ab59"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011PsE52UqcqGhpZ67U7Spb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still a regression (LogUp GKR: 528ms → 694ms). The 576 MB intermediates buffer exceeds the 72 MB L2 cache on RTX 4090, killing cache reuse. Let me cap the intermediates budget at 64 MB (fits in L2) so only the smallest AIRs get batched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":110065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1046},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aecb5aa0-2278-4de6-b698-d4c309499c34","uuid":"ffdd6b15-bb35-4727-ab77-227eab3830b8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011PsE52UqcqGhpZ67U7Spb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PxdBqxDPSmuiwNumHaRq1x","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs","old_string":"    // Memory budget check for batched intermediates: if > 2 GB, skip batching.\n    let batch_intermediates_bytes = total_batch_intermediates * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n    let use_batched = !batch_indices.is_empty() && batch_intermediates_bytes <= 2_000_000_000;\n    tracing::info!(\n        batch_eligible = batch_indices.len(),\n        non_batch = non_batch_indices.len(),\n        batch_intermediates_mb = batch_intermediates_bytes / (1024 * 1024),\n        use_batched,\n        \"GKR input eval batching decision\"\n    );","new_string":"    // Memory budget: cap at 64 MB so intermediates fit in L2 cache (72 MB on RTX 4090).\n    // Exceeding L2 destroys the cache reuse that makes the per-stream approach fast.\n    const MAX_BATCH_INTERMEDIATES_BYTES: usize = 64 * 1024 * 1024;\n    let batch_intermediates_bytes = total_batch_intermediates * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n    let use_batched =\n        !batch_indices.is_empty() && batch_intermediates_bytes <= MAX_BATCH_INTERMEDIATES_BYTES;\n\n    // If over budget, move batch-eligible items back to non-batch.\n    if !use_batched && !batch_indices.is_empty() {\n        non_batch_indices.clear();\n        non_batch_indices.extend(0..work_items.len());\n        batch_indices.clear();\n    }"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":110065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1046},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id"