{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WXHGdQigHrdeNh1vxejeT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pj9nP48d6gaeGWEvEjuJn8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nBatched descriptor-array GLOBAL-mode GKR input evaluation\n\nAdd a batched CUDA kernel for GLOBAL-mode GKR input evaluation that\nprocesses multiple small AIRs (height <= TASK_SIZE) in a single kernel\nlaunch using per-AIR descriptors and BlockCtx mapping.\n\nCUDA changes:\n- BatchGkrInputDesc struct with per-AIR pointers and metadata\n- BatchBlockCtx struct for block-to-AIR mapping\n- batched_gkr_input_eval_kernel with interleaved intermediates layout\n- _batched_gkr_input_eval C launcher\n\nRust changes:\n- BatchGkrInputDesc and BatchGkrInputBlockCtx FFI structs\n- batched_gkr_input_eval safe wrapper\n- Modified log_gkr_input_evals() to partition work items, build flat\n  device buffers for partition_ptrs/public_values, and orchestrate\n  batched + multi-stream paths concurrently\n- 64 MB L2 cache budget cap on batch intermediates (fallback to\n  per-stream path when exceeded)\n- Height normalization for batch-eligible AIRs with lifted heights\n\nThe optimization does not improve performance: at APC 300, the ~211\nbatch-eligible AIRs require 576 MB of intermediates, far exceeding the\n72 MB L2 cache and destroying the cache reuse that makes the per-stream\nsequential approach fast. The 64 MB budget cap effectively disables\nbatching for all significant workloads.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit implementation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_read_input_tokens":126293,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157},"output_tokens":56,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aecb5aa0-2278-4de6-b698-d4c309499c34","uuid":"193db92e-cddf-44ac-a50e-f8c2336c3052"}
